<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details). The disposition twin of
        Opportunity.Primary_LOI__c and the sibling of Disposition__c.Primary_NDA__c, whose
        file this one copies. THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a
        comment above &lt;CustomField&gt; breaks `sf` at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        🔴 THIS FIELD IS WHAT MAKES THE NATIVE LOI DETAILS SECTION POSSIBLE AT ALL. A FlexiPage
        fieldInstance cannot traverse a relationship, but a FORMULA field can - so the five
        LOI_*__c formula fields in this folder read through this lookup and the FlexiPage names
        them as ordinary Record. fields. Without the lookup there is nothing for those formulas
        to span, which is exactly why the retired c:dispositionChildDetails LWC existed.

        ⚠ IT RETRACTS A CLAIM THIS REPO MADE IN WRITING ON 2026-08-25, EARLIER THE SAME DAY.
        Disposition_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml and DispositionStageEntryService.cls both
        argued, verbatim, "THERE IS NO Primary_LOI__c AND NO Primary_PSA__c on Disposition__c -
        verified against objects/Disposition__c/fields/". That was true when written and is
        false now. Every place that reasoned FROM it has been rewritten in the same change,
        not left to be rediscovered.

        THE STAMP IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT BOOKKEEPING, exactly as on Primary_NDA__c.
        DispositionStageEntryService's LOI block writes this through
        DispositionPrimaryChildStampQueueable when it auto-creates the disposition LOI. A row
        whose stamp is missing renders a BLANK Details section at the LOI stage - not an error,
        which is the failure shape this repo keeps paying for. Rows created before this field
        existed are covered by the one-off backfill in manifest/native-loi-psa/.

        relationshipName is PrimaryDispositions, matching Primary_NDA__c's choice for the same
        reason: LOI__c already carries PrimaryOpportunities (Opportunity.Primary_LOI__c) and
        LOIs (LOI__c.Disposition__c), and a child relationship name must be unique per object.

        deleteConstraint is SetNull, matching both twins: deleting an LOI must clear the
        pointer, never cascade into the disposition.

        🔴 FLS DIVERGES FROM Primary_NDA__c ON PURPOSE, AND THE REASON IS THE BACKFILL.
        Primary_NDA__c is read-only in every set because its trigger is its only writer. This
        field has a SECOND writer - the one-off `sf data update record` backfill, which runs in
        USER mode and is refused outright on a field the running user cannot edit. So
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit carries editable = true here and DPEG_Disposition_View stays
        read-only. A lookup CAN carry editable = true; a formula field cannot (hard deploy
        error), which is why the nine LOI_*/PSA_* formulas beside it are read-only in both.
    -->
    <fullName>Primary_LOI__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The primary LOI for this disposition - stamped by the LOI stage-entry automation and spanned by the LOI_*__c formula fields that the LOI-stage Details section renders.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Set automatically when the disposition LOI is created. It points the LOI Details section at the right LOI, so it is not maintained by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Primary LOI</label>
    <referenceTo>LOI__c</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Dispositions (Primary LOI)</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>PrimaryDispositions</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
